  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "brief-summary",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -110,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "NutriQuest \u2014 cutesy, chibi-anime-style iOS mockups.\nAccent color follows the selected character (light tint); grey when none is selected; falls back to the best unselected character's color otherwise. Toggle \"accentColor\" + \"colorMode\" on any screen to preview.\nCollection card outlines now show all 7 rarity tiers (common/uncommon/rare/epic/legendary/mythic/secret) as a filled band, not a stroke. Chibi characters carry a small stat-type badge (protein/fiber/vitamin/hydration).\nScan, Gym Check and Connect Apple Watch each have a state tweak (stage/step) to preview their flow; Battle has a \"fatigued\" toggle; Collection has a \"loading\" toggle for the skeleton state.",
      "page": "page-screens"
    },
    {
      "id": "ui-kit-summary",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -110,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "UI Kit \u2014 the design system extracted from the screens: colors, elevation tokens, type scale, reusable components, character-building blocks, and every per-screen state (States sheet), including the generic Loading/Empty/Locked/Success patterns.",
      "page": "page-ui-kit"
    }
  ],
